     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks like a possible error.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5100 mg/day. The labeled maximum is 2550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin and 2000 mg/day for extended-release. At 5100 mg/day, this would be about double the maximum, and the risk of lactic acidosis rises with excess dosing. Normal kidney and liver function don't change that ceiling.\n\nCommon regimens for comparison:\n- 500 mg PO TID (1500 mg/day)\n- 850 mg PO TID (2550 mg/day, the maximum IR dose)\n- 1000 mg PO BID (2000 mg/day)\n\nCould you confirm which you intend? If you meant a different dose or frequency, tell me and I'll enter it. If 1700 mg TID is intentional, please confirm and I'll enter it as written, though I'd recommend checking the dose against the pharmacy's protocol first."
      }
